# fixedbugs, defect 2351, lane b25-pkgc, 2026-11-08.
#
# A fetched package's constants are read from clang's front end, its constant
# evaluator's value of each as an enumerator under `-fsyntax-only`, and never
# by the probe that compiles and runs the package's unit, which ran its
# header's constructors at build (panel 235's R9, its C5). What that reading
# cannot value is refused, never run: a float, which no enumerator holds; an
# enumerator, whose own initialiser it folds unjudged; a division C leaves
# undefined; an object, which is no integer constant expression. `PK_FINE`,
# an integer constant expression C defines, is read and told nothing.
use <pk>/pk

function main()
    print(pk.sum())
